    <statement><p>The plane that passes through the point <m>\left(2,4,-4\right)</m> and is
perpendicular to both <m>4x+2y+5z = -25</m> and
<m>4x-4y = -4</m> has
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/> as its implicit equation.</p>
</statement>
    <hint><B>Hint: </B>How do the normal vectors for two
perpendicular planes relate to each other?
</hint>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>24z-\left(20x+20y\right) = -216</m>
      </p>
